16. Security, Compliance & Trust
⦁	Least-privilege roles: Owner/Admin/Support/Operator (if needed) and User; each role permissions explicitly defined।
⦁	Never store plaintext passwords or full payment credentials; use auth provider and secure secrets।
⦁	Do not expose other users' profile, payment receipt, phone, wallet ledger or order details through public queries.
⦁	Terms, privacy, refund, product delivery, subscription account sharing, regional restrictions and ad disclosures clearly visible.
⦁	Do not sell unauthorized accounts, stolen credentials, fake engagement, or services violating platform terms/law.
⦁	Rate limit login, OTP, checkout, referral claims, reward claims, uploads and support forms.
⦁	Use HTTPS only, secure cookies/session, CSRF protection where applicable, CSP and allowlisted third-party scripts.
⦁	Admin changes and financial operations must be auditable and reversible where appropriate.
